        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Elbridge, New York\n- People: Elbridge Gerry\n- Roles: Vice President of the United States\n- Topics: United States census, place naming\n\nFacts:\n- Elbridge Gerry served as the fifth Vice President of the United States from March 1813 until his death in November 1814.\n- Elbridge Gerry was a Democratic-Republican and one of the signers of the Declaration of Independence.\n- The town of Elbridge, New York, is named after Elbridge Gerry.\n- Elbridge, New York, had a population of 5,922 at the 2010 census.",
